de", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "components_contactform_contactform", "label": "ContactForm component (mailto: submission, optional backend upgrade)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_messages_structure", "label": "messages/*.json translation files \u2014 identical key structure across fr/en/ar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_calendly_integration", "label": "Calendly booking integration via react-calendly InlineWidget, mounted post-hydration in reserved 700px container", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "lib_site_calendly_url", "label": "CALENDLY_URL constant (lib/site.ts) \u2014 default Calendly link, overridable via env var", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_calendly_env_var", "label": "NEXT_PUBLIC_CALENDLY_URL environment variable \u2014 swap Calendly account/event without touching code", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_calendly_event_name_mismatch", "label": "Calendly event is titled '30 Minute Meeting' while the site copy says '\u00c9change d\u00e9couverte \u2014 30 minutes'; rename on Calendly's side, not a code fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_calendly_free_tier_colors", "label": "Calendly embed pageSettings send #1D4ED8 as primary color but Calendly ignores custom theming on free-tier accounts, so its default theme + 'Powered by Calendly' banner render instead; code already correct for a future paid upgrade", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_wcag_color_deviation", "label": "Brief demanded #94A3B8 for tertiary text AND WCAG AA compliance \u2014 incompatible (2.46:1 contrast vs 4.5:1 required); token ink-3 uses #64748B (4.56:1) instead, one step down the same slate ramp, with #94A3B8 kept as ink-faint for non-text illustration strokes only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_signature_measurement_rule", "label": "Signature 'measurement rule' element under the hero title, graduated 'Web \u00b7 IA \u00b7 Data \u00b7 IoT \u00b7 Industrie' \u2014 Mohammed's positioning as an amplitude ('web to industrial field'), drawn as an instrument rather than stated in prose; self-draws once on load and mirrors in RTL", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_project_visuals_schemas", "label": "Project visuals are functional schemas, not generic mockups \u2014 each abstracts what the real system does (search, sensor threshold curve, weighing ticket, compliance matrix), inline SVG, site palette only, zero image weight", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_services_section_band", "label": "Single white band on the whole page is the Services section, marking the pivot from CV to commercial offer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_motion_system", "label": "Motion system prioritizes care over quantity per the brief's 'sober use only' constraint \u2014 few, fully orchestrated movements, none decorative; single shared expo-out easing [0.16,1,0.3,1] and duration scale from lib/motion.ts; only transform/opacity animated, never layout, so zero reflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "lib_motion_motion", "label": "lib/motion.ts \u2014 shared easing curve and duration scale for all site animation", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_hero_css_only", "label": "Hero is pure CSS, not JavaScript \u2014 title, tagline, buttons and rule animate via keyframes so the most important content never depends on a script to become visible (a stalled JS animation would otherwise leave the hero blank); Hero, SplitWords, RangeRule stay server components", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_lazymotion_decision", "label": "LazyMotion + m components load only the domAnimation feature set instead of the full Framer Motion build (components import m, not motion, enforced by 'strict'), cutting First Load JS from 168kB to 144kB despite adding the whole motion system", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_motion_accessibility", "label": "MotionConfig reducedMotion='user' neutralizes Framer transform animations, and a CSS killswitch in globals.css neutralizes keyframes including delays \u2014 otherwise a prefers-reduced-motion visitor would stare at hidden content through the longest delay before it snaps into view", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_header_reading_progress", "label": "Header reading-progress hairline on the bottom edge \u2014 same measurement idea as the hero rule, applied to the document; active-section marker traces itself under the current link", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_card_hover_hairline", "label": "Card hover state: 2px lift, short shadow, and an accent hairline that traces along the top edge on hover \u2014 same graduation vocabulary as the hero rule", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "lib_routing_routing", "label": "lib/routing.ts \u2014 locale routing configuration (fr/en/ar)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "middleware_middleware", "label": "middleware.ts \u2014 locale-prefix routing (/fr default, /en, /ar)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_rtl_handling", "label": "RTL support is structural, not just textual \u2014 grids, timeline spine (moved right), directional icons, hero rule and its graduations all flip via logical CSS properties (start/end, ms/me, ps/pe); spaced caps neutralized under [lang='ar'], .tech-tag uses unicode-bidi:plaintext with an LRM mark for '.NET' strings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "app_locale_opengraphimage_rtl", "label": "rtl() helper in app/[locale]/opengraph-image.tsx \u2014 manually reorders Arabic tokens because Satori renders Arabic glyphs but does not apply the bidi algorithm", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_og_image_bidi_workaround", "label": "Per-locale OG image via next/og \u2014 Satori draws Arabic glyphs correctly but skips the bidi algorithm, so the 'ar' card manually reverses its tokens and stays on one line via the rtl() helper; drop the helper if a future Satori version fixes bidi (the site itself is unaffected since the browser handles bidi)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_verifications", "label": "Pre-launch verification checklist: clean build/lint across 3 prerendered locales, single h1 and unbroken heading order, no horizontal overflow at 375/1440px LTR+RTL, timeline accordion aria state, form aria-invalid/aria-describedby, prefers-reduced-motion respected, hero word-split preserves textContent in FR/AR, progress bar checked at 0/25/50/75/100%; scroll reveals and animated schema playback unverifiable in the dev environment (tab stuck at visibilityState:hidden) \u2014 final states validated via the Web Animations API instead", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_accent_color_1d4ed8", "label": "#1D4ED8 accent blue \u2014 brief-compliant token (6.4:1 contrast, 6.7:1 white-on-blue), used for the hero rule's high graduation and Calendly pageSettings prima